      "title": "Cycling in Modern Cities",
      "text": "In recent years, many city planners have been working hard to make urban areas more cycle-friendly. One of the main goals is to (1) ______ traffic congestion by encouraging people to leave their cars at home. Cycling is not only a great way to get some exercise, but it is also much (2) ______ for the environment than driving. Many cities have now introduced dedicated bike lanes, which help to (3) ______ cyclists feel much safer when they are on the road. However, there are still challenges to overcome. Some people (4) ______ that the current infrastructure is not enough to support a large number of daily commuters. Despite this, the popularity of cycling continues to grow as more people (5) ______ the benefits of a healthier lifestyle. Experts believe that if cities continue to invest in better facilities, cycling will (6) ______ an essential part of urban transport in the future.",
